## Behaviour after the fix

- Click **Thread** on any message → a new chat is created with `parent_id = chat.id` and `message_id = message.doc_id`, inheriting `board`, `column`, `mode`, `file_list` and `profiles`, then it is opened (dockview panel on desktop, route on mobile, or the vibe chat panel).
- Click **Thread** again on the same message (or after a reload) → the existing thread is found (parent children first, then any loaded chat with that `message_id`) and opened — no duplicates.
- Chats without a board / with an incomplete kanban no longer throw; the thread is still created and opened (it simply isn't added as a board card).
- No model run is triggered on creation: the thread is empty and the user writes the first message.
- The message bubble keeps rendering its own content; the reply counter badge (`N replies`) is the navigation entry point.

## Accessibility notes

- The Thread button keeps the existing `tooltip tooltip-bottom` + `data-tip="Thread"` pattern; it remains a real `<button>` inside the header's focus order, so Tab + Enter still works.
- The replies badge in the message body is a native `<button>` with visible text (`N replies`) — not color-only — so it is announced with meaningful content by screen readers.

